r['interpretation']+=' Q3 (outflow): dense gas (HCN and HCO+ 3-2) is detected in the blue wing 1.9" (370 pc) south of the S nucleus (HCN 12.6 sigma, HCO+ 5 sigma), in the location, direction and sense of the blue lobe of the edge-on southern bipolar outflow (Sakamoto+2014; Michiyama+2018), with a red counterpart toward OF-Red between the nuclei and no wing at N (pole-on outflow, <1-2% of core). The lobe shows a blueshift gradient perpendicular to the E-W rotation gradient and an HCN/HCO+ 3-2 ratio rising from 0.6 at lobe core velocities to >=2 at -300..-400 km/s (1.7+-0.35 in the wing), ~4x S and ~2x N, while the red lobe is nuclear-like (1.0+-0.2). This matches Michiyama+2018 (dense-gas fraction rising with velocity) and resembles the high HCN/HCO+ shells of Nishimura+2024 (shock chemistry), but the data do not prove the origin; RADEX (tentative) points to an HCN/HCO+ column or abundance ratio >~10 rather than density. M_dense ~6e6 Msun (factor 2-3) in the blue wing.'
